    "text": "And it shows up on the battlefield. Ukrainian officials say they keep finding foreign components inside Russian drones and missiles, some stamped with manufacturing dates from twenty twenty five and even twenty twenty six. These aren't old stockpiles from before the war. They were made, sold and smuggled long after the sanctions began. Many of those drones are Russia's own version of Iran's Shahed, built at a giant factory complex called Alabuga, hundreds of miles east of Moscow, turning out thousands of drones a year. And inside them, again and again, investigators find the same thing, Western chips.",
